/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 3.1 The Twelve Tense-Aspect System in Technical Communication) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Scientific writing demands precise tense-aspect selection to reflect the chronological) Tj
T*
(status and empirical validity of findings.) Tj
T*
(* Present Tense System:) Tj
T*
(- Simple Present: Used for universal scientific truths, established natural laws,) Tj
T*
(and general axioms: "Water boils at 100 deg C under atmospheric pressure." Stative) Tj
T*
(verbs \(know, believe, consist, contain\) cannot be used in continuous aspects \(*is) Tj
T*
(containing is ungrammatical\).) Tj
T*
(- Present Continuous: Ongoing dynamic events at the time of speaking: "The) Tj
T*
(temperature is rising steadily.") Tj
T*
(- Present Perfect: Action initiated in the past with direct relevance or) Tj
T*
(continuation into the present: "Researchers have discovered a novel thermostable) Tj
T*
(Taq polymerase." Uses 'Since' \(specific point in time: since 2018\) vs. 'For') Tj
T*
(\(duration: for five years\).) Tj
T*
(- Present Perfect Continuous: Continuous action extending from past to present:) Tj
T*
("The culture has been fermenting for 72 hours.") Tj
T*
(* Past Tense System:) Tj
T*
(- Simple Past: Completed actions at a specific, stated past time; standard tense) Tj
T*
(for Materials and Methods and Experimental Results sections: "The solution was) Tj
T*
(centrifuged at 10,000 rpm for 15 minutes.") Tj
T*
(- Past Continuous: Ongoing background action interrupted by another past event:) Tj
T*
("The bioreactor was operating normally when the power failed.") Tj
T*
(- Past Perfect: An action completed prior to another past action \(anteriority\):) Tj
T*
("The cells had entered apoptosis before the inhibitor was administered.") Tj
T*
(* Future Tense System: Expressed via modal auxiliaries \(will, shall\) or periphrastic) Tj
T*
(forms \(is going to\).) Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
() Tj
T*
/F2 9.5 Tf
(>> 3.2 The Four Conditional Clause Architectures) Tj
T*
/F1 9 Tf
() Tj
T*
(Conditionals consist of a dependent conditional clause \(if-clause / protasis\) and an) Tj
T*
(independent consequence clause \(main clause / apodosis\).) Tj
T*
(* Zero Conditional \(Universal Scientific Truths & Invariant Causality\):) Tj
T*
(- Structure: If + Simple Present, ... Simple Present.) Tj
T*
(- Example: "If water reaches 100 deg C at 1 atm, it boils." \(Invariable) Tj
T*
(thermodynamic law\).) Tj
T*
(* First Conditional \(Real / Probable Future Event\):) Tj
T*
(- Structure: If + Simple Present, ... will / can / may + Base Verb \(V1\).) Tj
T*
(- Example: "If the fermenter temperature exceeds 40 deg C, the microbial enzymes) Tj
T*
(will denature.") Tj
T*
(* Second Conditional \(Hypothetical / Unreal Present or Future Event\):) Tj
T*
ET

